Key Insights

1. Global COVID-19 Cases
The global total cases chart shows that the overall reported COVID-19 case burden was highest when viewing the World aggregate. This represents the combined reported cases across countries.

2. Daily Cases Trend
The daily cases trend shows a major peak around 2022, indicating a period of increased reported COVID-19 cases in the dataset.

3. Daily Deaths Trend
The daily deaths trend shows a major peak around 2021, highlighting a period of increased reported COVID-19 deaths.

Conclusion

The dashboard helps compare reported COVID-19 cases and deaths over time and understand the global impact of the pandemic. These trends are based on reported data and may be affected by differences in testing and reporting between countries.
